From f78f97f8ab69b90a1a978ce2b098f1a0e0c0dbb6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Orbit Dev <dev@orbit.invalid>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 18:20:31 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 16/30] feat(orbit): windows, Start Menu apps, show desktop,
 volume and power API

New mTLS routes: GET /orbit/windows, POST /orbit/windows/activate?id=
(404 not_found, 409 denied), POST /orbit/desktop, GET /orbit/apps,
POST /orbit/apps/launch?id= (orbit_windows); POST /orbit/power?action=
shutdown|restart|sleep|logoff|lock (orbit_power, 400 on unknown action,
logs "[Orbit] power <action> pedido por <device>"); POST /orbit/volume
?level=0..100 (clamped) and/or mute=0|1 (input_kbd).

Platform calls sit behind WindowPlatform/PowerPlatform (fakes in tests).
Windows side: visible titled top-level windows (no tool windows, cloaked
or host-owned windows), activate restores then SetForegroundWindow with an
empty-mouse-input retry, refusing higher-integrity targets; ToggleDesktop
with Win+D fallback; .lnk shortcuts from the common and the logged-in
user's Start Menu (user token when SYSTEM), opened via explorer.exe through
platf::run_command (runs as the user); Core Audio volume; shutdown/restart
via InitiateSystemShutdownExW (apps not forced), sleep via SetSuspendState
(deferred), logoff via ExitWindowsEx/WTSLogoffSession, lock via
LockWorkStation (rundll32 as the user when SYSTEM).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
